[0.025, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m ▐\u001b[48;2;0;0;0m▛███▜\u001b[49m▌\u001b[39m   \u001b[1mClaude Code\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mv2.0.43\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m▝▜\u001b[48;2;0;0;0m█████\u001b[49m▛▘\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSonnet 4.5 · Claude Enterprise\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m  ▘▘ ▝▝  \u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m/Users/wolffiex/code/qcon-2025-ai-speed/main\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m> /add-dir \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mWorkspace dialog dismissed\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m> @static/presentation.md read this file \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m I've read the presentation file! This is a fascinating talk about \"Engineering at AI Speed\"\r\n  for QCon San Francisco 2025.\r\n\r\n  The presentation tells three compelling stories from building Claude Code:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m🎯 Episode I: Rebuilding Input\u001b[22m\r\n  - Started with 333 lines of virtual Cursor class (Dec 2024)\r\n  - Evolved over 9 months through Vim mode, Unicode handling (graphemes, NFC), and performance\r\n  op"]
[0.000, "o", "timization\r\n  - Ended at 945 lines with 490+ tests\r\n  - Key lesson: AI + comprehensive tests made complexity manageable\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m🐚 Episode II: Reimagining Shell\u001b[22m\r\n  - Pivoted from PersistentShell (773 lines, sequential) to transient shells (346 lines,\r\n  parallel)\r\n  - Discovered non-obvious \"snapshot\" pattern (310 lines) to capture user environment\r\n  - Total: 656 lines vs original 773, but way more extensible\r\n  - Enabled features like sandboxing easily\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m💀 Episode III: Reversing SQLite\u001b[22m\r\n  - Replaced working JSONL with SQLite\r\n  - 15 days from launch to complete removal\r\n  - Hit foundational issues: native deps, locking, migrations, version skew\r\n  - Reverted to 277 lines of simple JSONL\r\n  - Key lesson: Fast reversal is valuable\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCentral thesis\u001b[22m: With AI, implementation cost → zero, so feedback loops become everything. Ship\r\n   continuously, make reversal cheap, and optimize for learning speed over judgment quality.\r\n\r\n  What would you like to do with this presentation?\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?25l\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n> \u001b[7mT\u001b[27m\u001b[2mry \"write a test for parser.ts\"\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m-- INSERT --\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[?2026l"]
